{
 "_doc": "Hand fit of the downloaded gun models (T-089, UPDATE_05 section 2), read by WeaponGLB on top of models.json. Rig space everywhere: metres, barrel along -Z, +Y up, origin at the right-hand grip. Per weapon: extra_rot [deg xyz] and extra_offset [m] after the models.json normalisation (the converter's trigger_center lands 8 mm ahead / 6 mm below the origin by default), scale (overrides native.scale), grip_native (the pack-space point that becomes the origin instead of the trigger), pivots {Part: [x,y,z]} (hinges for Cover / Barrels, the bolt axis for Bolt; default = the part's centre), parent {Part: Parent} (the Webley cylinder under its barrels), rename {node: Part}, hide [node], borrow {Part: {asset, node, offset}} (a part from another converted asset), part_offset / part_scale / part_scale_about {Part: [x,y,z]} (a part moved or cut down: the Garand clip into the receiver, the Sawed-Off barrels; scaled up: the Totenglocke's striker Hammer and Pawl, T-098), warp {Part: {z0, z1, dy}} (T-098: every vertex of the part behind z1 moves dy up, easing in from z0, rig space: the STG44 stock dropped below the sight line), muzzle / sight_rear / sight_front / left_hand [x,y,z] (defaults from a vertex scan: bbox front on the bore, the highest point in the front quarter, the highest point on the receiver), sight_rear_on / sight_front_on (the group a sight rides on: the Slide when there is one, else root), lh_axis z|y, lh_radius, grip_r [x,y,z], grip_lean deg, grip_r_radius, port [x,y,z], bore, no_bore, eye_relief (overrides weapons.json feel.eye_relief for this model: the cheek weld differs per model), empty {Part: [x,y,z]} (an empty node for a part the reload expects but the pack lacks), scope {y, z0, z1, r, base_y, mag} (a procedural scope on an iron-sighted model), kit_offset {slot: [x,y,z]} and kit_offset_front {slot: [x,y,z]} (the M1911 hand-fitted attachments, built for the procedural pistol, shifted onto the OGA one per slot; _front applies to parts ahead of z -0.08), stock_share (the rear share of the length the sight scan skips), shader {wear, grime, scratches, grain_scale, seed, bluing [r,g,b], wood {material: 0..1}, metal_parts [Part], wood_parts [Part], palette_remap {cell index: [r,g,b]} (an OGA palette cell repainted for this gun, cell = row * 8 + column, sRGB: the STG44 stock's crimson to walnut, T-098)}. frost_by_map: the rime uniform per map id (WeaponShader). Fit sheets: tools/glb_fit_shots.sh. wonder {crucible_parts [Part], materials {glass|fluid|glow|coil_glow|emitter|arc|runes|halo|orb: {color, hot, strength, tint, refraction}}, upgraded {energy, shader {weapon-shader uniform: value}, colors {material: [r,g,b]}, strength {material: k}}, part_metas {Part: {meta: [x,y,z]}}} (T-090: the wonder weapons modelled by us; WonderLook).",
